"A procedure whose effect a process may have may cross into another
 thread, so its Rust is `Send + Sync`, and what it holds must be too
 (C102): this one holds a reference it never touches, which FX-26 lets
 cross, judging what it does, and Rust would not, judging what it holds."
(define f (subr (alloc @c) () (subr pure () int))
  (lambda ()
    (let ((r (the (ref int @c) (new 0))))
      (lambda () (begin r 1)))))
